  displayName: Lenape
  leader: Tamanend
  date: c. 1683
  biography: Tamanend was a Lenape village sachem documented in late seventeenth-century Pennsylvania. He was not a king ruling all Lenape communities.
  region: Delaware Valley; present-day Pennsylvania, New Jersey, Delaware and nearby areas.
  terrain:
  - Broadleaf Forest
  - Mixed Forest
  - Prairie
  goods:
  - Food
  - Fur
  jobs:
  - Farmers
  - Fur Trappers
  rival: Susquehannock
  scenarioAggression: Low
  contextNote: Susquehannock rivalry refers to earlier conflicts in the 1620s-1630s, not a claim that Tamanend fought them in 1683. Food and Fur match farming and winter hunting.
  sources:
  - https://www.ustwp.org/government/boards-commissions/historical-advisory-board/chief-tamanend/
